    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise log1p with exponent reduction and a short odd polynomial.\n2: \n3: Original synthetic Triton implementation, not an upstream bug reproduction.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: import torch\n6: import triton\n7: import triton.language as tl\n8: \n9: \n10: @triton.jit\n11: def _log1p_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n12:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n13:     active = index < N\n14:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n15:     u = 1.0 + x\n16:     correction = tl.div_rn(x - (u - 1.0), u)\n17:     encoding = u.to(tl.uint32, bitcast=True)\n18:     exponent = ((encoding >> 23) & 255).to(tl.int32) - 127\n19:     mantissa = ((encoding & 0x007fffff) | 0x3f800000).to(tl.float32, bitcast=True)\n20:     upper = mantissa > 1.65\n21:     mantissa = tl.where(upper, mantissa * 0.5, mantissa)\n22:     exponent = exponent + upper.to(tl.int32)\n23:     z = tl.div_rn(mantissa - 1.0, mantissa + 1.0)\n24:     square = z * z\n25:     polynomial = 0.142857\n26:     polynomial = polynomial * square + 0.2\n27:     polynomial = polynomial * square + 0.33333\n28:     polynomial = 1.0 + square * polynomial\n29:     local_log = (2.0 * z) * polynomial\n30:     high = exponent.to(tl.float32) * 0.69313812256\n31:     low = exponent.to(tl.float32) * 0.0000090580006145\n32:     value = high + (local_log + (low + correction))\n33:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n34: \n35: \n36: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n37:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n38:     def require(condition, message):\n39:         if not condition:\n40:             raise ValueError(message)\n41: \n42:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n43:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n44:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n45:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n46:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n47:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n48:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n49:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n50:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n51:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n52:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n53:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n54:     require(bool((torch.isfinite(x) & (x > -1.0)).all().item()),\n55:             \"all input values must be finite and greater than -1\")\n56:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n57: \n58: \n59: def run(x):\n60:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor approximating log(1+x).\"\"\"\n61:     validate_inputs(x)\n62:     n = x.numel()\n63:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n64:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n65:         _log1p_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n66:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n67:     return output\n68: \n69: \n70: def reference(x):\n71:     \"\"\"Evaluate the mathematical target with the FP64 library log1p.\"\"\"\n72:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n73:     return torch.log1p(x.to(torch.float64))\n74: \n75: \n76: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n77:     \"\"\"Convenience examples only; all finite FP16 values greater than -1 are legal.\"\"\"\n78:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n79:     x = (4.0 * torch.rand((size,), generator=generator) - 0.75).to(torch.float16)\n80:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute log1p elementwise on stored FP16 values, returning FP32 output.\nThe mathematical target is target[i] = log(1 + x[i]), where log is the natural logarithm.\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- Every finite FP16 value strictly greater than -1 is legal. This includes both signed zeros, positive and negative subnormals, the representable value immediately above -1, and the largest finite FP16 value 65504. NaN, infinity and values at or below -1 are outside this domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided, contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False, is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode, without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x. Every output element must satisfy:\n\n  abs(actual[i] - log(1 + x[i])) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent. The target is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value. No particular range reduction, polynomial approximation or intermediate rounding is part of the mathematical target. Approximations are permitted if they satisfy this fixed absolute tolerance throughout the entire legal domain. Correctness is one verdict for the implementation, not a verdict per input, distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference() uses the FP64 library log1p and returns FP64; it accepts CPU inputs. make_inputs() supplies examples only. This is an original synthetic Triton implementation of a standard elementary function. It is not a reproduction of an upstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch 2.8.0, Triton 3.4.0.\n",
